In article <12569@netcom.UUCP> rcb@netcom.uucp (Roy Bixler) writes:
>kick the wall, lose maybe 2 or 3 hit-points, pray and get them all back and
>more.  Well, that was the first and only time I've ever seen kicking a wall
>take off 5 hit-points or more!  That seems kind of bogus to me, since I
>kicked the wall on purpose and I should have control over whether I kick
>it with all my might or just moderately hard.

I think the assumption that you always kick with all your might is okay.
For the most part you don't kick things to cause yourself damage.  If the
game could control how hard you kick, the feature would only be used to
lower your own hit points.  Of course, NetHack should be as lifelike as
possible, but we have to draw the line somewhere.  As for being lowered
five hit points, if your constitution is below 16 you can lose up to five
hit points at a shot (if your constitution is >= 16, you only lose up to
three hit points).
